: 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Error during confiugration:\n```sh\ncmake -S . -B buld\n```\n\nwith result:\n```sh\n[100%] Built target mavlink\nCMake Warning:\n  Ignoring empty string (\"\") provided on the command line.\n\n\nCMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:1 (cmake_minimum_required):\n  Compatibility with CMake < 3.5 has been removed from CMake.\n\n  Update the VERSION argument <min> value.  Or, use the <min>...<max> syntax\n  to tell CMake that the project requires at least <min> but has been updated\n  to work with policies introduced by <max> or earlier.\n\n  Or, add -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 to try configuring anyway.\n\n\n-- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!\nCMake Error at third_party/cmake/build_target.cmake:32 (message):\n  \n  /mnt/zyncdev/user/NovaLabs/Hammer/repos/mavlink/mavlink-tools/mavsdk/third_party/jsoncpp\n  failed to configure!\nCall Stack (most recent call first):\n  third_party/CMakeLists.txt:12 (build_target)\n\n\n-- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!\n```\n\nSounds like `third_party/jsoncpp/CMakeLists.txt` just should be updated to point to the cmake 3.5 at least. But I suggest change it to the same minimum cmake version, that used for root CMakeLists.txt for now: 3.13.\n\nSame suggestion for all other third_party components, that point to the cmake 3.1.\n\nAlso, jsoncpp must be updated itself. It provides `src/jsoncpp/jsoncppConfig.cmake.in` that points into CMake 3.0 policy. Newest version updates it: https://github.com/open-source-parsers/jsoncpp/blob/master/jsoncppConfig.cmake.in\n\nAnother solution, just set ENV variable `CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM` at the top-level CMakeLists.txt:\n```cmake\nset(ENV{CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM} 3.13)\n```\nor run configuration like:\n```sh\nenv CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.16 cmake -S . -B buld\n```\n", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "",